# Traefik dashboard HTTP basic-auth credentials, in standard htpasswd format
# (user:bcrypt-hash), one per line.
#
# This is a real file mount (not a compose env var) deliberately: a bcrypt
# hash is full of literal '$' characters, and routing that through
# docker compose's `.env` -> `${VAR}` interpolation is fragile — those
# dollar signs can get re-parsed as variable references and silently
# stripped. A mounted file sidesteps the problem entirely.
#
# Generate a line with:
#   docker run --rm httpd:alpine htpasswd -nbB admin 'your-password-here'
# then copy this file to dashboard-users.htpasswd (gitignored) with the
# real output, e.g.:
#   admin:$2y$05$abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXY
